---
/*
 * /styleguide/three/: the 3D runtime's test scene (SITE-05). Preview builds only, like /styleguide/
 * (a rest-parameter route, so getStaticPaths can return nothing in a public build).
 * A field of voxel cubes that rises with the scroll, in the first screen as a home page's opening scene
 * would be, and a second one far down the page for the "does not start while far away" check. The text
 * says what the scene shows, because the canvas is aria-hidden and nothing may be only in the 3D.
 */
import { PUBLIC } from "../../../../site.config";
import Scene from "../../../components/Scene.astro";
import Section from "../../../components/Section.astro";
import Page from "../../../layouts/Page.astro";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return PUBLIC ? [] : [{ params: { slug: undefined } }];
}
---

<Page
  title="3D test scene"
  description="The test scene for the CuePoint site's 3D runtime: a field of pixel cubes that rises as you scroll. Preview builds only."
  path="styleguide/three/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: "Home", path: "" },
    { label: "Style guide", path: "styleguide/" },
    { label: "3D test scene", path: "styleguide/three/" },
  ]}
>
  <Section id="scene" width="prose">
    <h1>Cubes that rise with the scroll</h1>
    <Scene name="cubes" priority />
    <p class="caption">
      The picture shows a square field of eleven by eleven blocks seen from above and to the side. The
      blocks at the center are tallest and the ones at the edges stay low. Their shadows fall hard on
      the floor, and each block is outlined in black. Scroll, and the blocks grow and the view turns.
      If 3D does not run on your device, this is a still picture of the same field.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section id="between" heading="Room to scroll" width="prose">
    <p class="run-up">
      The 3D starts only when a scene is within a screen of where you are and you have scrolled,
      touched or pressed a key. This page has a second field far below, which stays a picture until you
      get close.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section id="far" heading="A second field" width="prose">
    <Scene name="cubes" />
    <p class="caption tall">
      The same field of blocks again. Nothing on this page depends on the picture or on the 3D.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Page>

<style>
  .caption {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }
  .run-up {
    min-height: 220vh;
  }
  /* room to scroll far past the scene, so its loop can be seen to sleep */
  .tall {
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
</style>
